* Buck converter with a load step: the load resistor changes from 6 ohm to 3 ohm at 4 ms
* and the voltage reference changes from 12 V to 9 V at 7 ms - no extra switches or sources needed.
.title Buck converter with value changes
.param vin=48 fsw=50k
Vin   in  0   DC {vin}
S1    in  sw  gate
D1    0   sw
L1    sw  out 100u
C1    out 0   220u
Rload out 0   6
* ---- control circuit
B1 VSENSOR  vo out 0
B2 ISENSOR  il_raw L1
B3 ZOH      il il_raw fs={fsw}
B4 CONST    vref value=12
B5 SUM      verr vref vo signs=+-
B6 PI       iref verr kp=0.7 ki=700 lo=0 hi=10
B7 SUM      ierr iref il signs=+-
B8 PI       duty ierr kp=0.065 ki=200 lo=0 hi=0.9
B9 PWM      gate duty freq={fsw}
* ---- run-time value changes
.change 4m Rload 3
.change 7m vref 9
.tran 0.2u 10m
.plot V(out),vref I(L1)
.measure mean V(out)
.window 0.5m
.end
